"""Speech module: speaking with altered auditory feedback (formant or pitch shifts, masking, delay), one row per utterance.

Defined with the first speech dataset (Zeng2025_JExpPsycholGen). Columns hold the authors' own per-utterance values.
Produced formants are kept in the unit the authors shared them in (Hz or mel), never converted between the two here,
because the mel formula used to make a shared value is not always stated. The perturbation itself is in the CORE
columns (pert_type, pert_value, pert_unit, feedback); shift_f1 and shift_f2 split a formant shift into its F1 and F2
parts, which one pert_value cannot hold for two-dimensional shifts."""

DESCRIPTION = ("Speech production with altered auditory feedback: one row per utterance, with the acoustic values the authors "
               "measured (formants, f0, intensity, duration), the word and segment they measured and over which window, "
               "the per-formant feedback shift in force, and the masking noise and feedback delay of the setup.")

# (column, type, values or units, description)
